#X obj 674 11 env2array;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 356 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 Renders an envelope into an array \, filling the array
with the values of the envelope over time. The rendering mode controls
how the envelope length is matched to the array size: *fit* stretches
the envelope to fit the array \, *resize* resizes the array to match
the envelope length \, and *raw* writes the envelope into the array
up to the array length \, discarding the rest of the envelope.;
#X text 240 214 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 239 • Visualizing envelopesy.;
#X text 250 264 • Preparing an envelope for playback — rendering an
envelope into an array so it can be played back as an audio rate signal
via [tabplay~] \, for applying the same shape at audio rate.;
#X text 250 334 • Integration with array-based processing — using the
resulting array as a source for other array objects (for example \,
[array.convolve] \, [array.stretch] or [array.play~]) that work with
array data rather than envelopes.;
